{
  "_id": "259Ey7LXgqL7ZDGJ8XK1vBJmZrh",
  "_type": "Doc",
  "_index": "a0",
  "title": "Configuration",
  "navigationTitle": "",
  "body": [
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "All configuration lives in `cms.ts`, which exports the `cms` instance your pages query and the handler serves. `alinea init` creates it in the project root, or in `src/` when that folder exists. Alinea also finds it as `cms.tsx`, `cms.js` or `cms.jsx`; pass `--config` to the "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "CLI",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "2bRPphjzKp0th73W5AIX4MbwCAC",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "m5KGP-I5smg2S8o4A-j15"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " to use another location."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2a4tC7lBmNMZUuJDec7zsG4st62",
      "code": "import {Config, Field} from 'alinea'\nimport {createCMS} from 'alinea/next'\n\nconst Page = Config.document('Page', {\n  fields: {\n    body: Field.richText('Body')\n  }\n})\n\nexport const cms = createCMS({\n  schema: {Page},\n  workspaces: {\n    main: Config.workspace('Main', {\n      source: 'content',\n      mediaDir: 'public/media',\n      roots: {\n        pages: Config.root('Pages', {contains: ['Page']}),\n        media: Config.media()\n      }\n    })\n  },\n  baseUrl: {\n    development: 'http://localhost:3000',\n    production: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL ?? 'https://example.com'\n  },\n  handlerUrl: '/api/cms',\n  adminPath: '/admin',\n  preview: true,\n  enableDrafts: true\n})",
      "fileName": "cms.ts",
      "language": "tsx",
      "compact": false
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Import `createCMS` from `alinea/next` in a Next.js project. It accepts the options below and returns the `cms` object with the query methods (`find`, `first`, `get`, `count`), `cms.previews` and `cms.workspaces`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Required options"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "required-options"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`schema`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "schema"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "An object of all your types, keyed by name: `{Page, BlogPost}`. The key is the type name stored in content files and used in `contains` and `_type`, so don't rename it once content exists. See "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Schema",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "2YkhKab77FPvVbFuEKDFvTCeQqA",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "267KTV8uPHIdZgFUQvJf06sfm4h"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`workspaces`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "workspaces"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "An object of "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "workspaces",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "2YkhLyWRcJ1TaBwxb1l8MIeWbGP",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "259EzPfnSUaKOrNL1S2bpIpMdKl"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ", at least one. Keys may only use `a-z`, `A-Z`, `0-9` and `_`. With more than one workspace, each `source` folder must be named after its key and all of them must sit in the same parent folder."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`handlerUrl`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "handlerurl"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The URL of the API route that serves the dashboard and media files: the route that exports `createHandler` from `alinea/next`. `alinea init` sets it to `/api/cms` and creates `app/(alinea)/api/cms/route.ts`. A relative URL is resolved against `baseUrl`. Without it `alinea dev`, `alinea build` and your site throw `Missing handlerUrl in Alinea config`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`baseUrl`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "baseurl"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The URL of your website, either one string or one per environment: `{development, production}`, picked by `NODE_ENV`. A value without a protocol gets `https://`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "`alinea build` exits with `No baseUrl was set for the production build` when there is no production URL."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "In production your site reaches the handler at `handlerUrl` resolved against this URL, to check for new content. That includes `next start` on your machine, which talks to the production URL."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Most projects read the production URL from an environment variable, see "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Environment variables",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkBBqZ0RopEe3YR2clripNOAub",
              "_link": "url",
              "href": "#environment-variables"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " below."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Dashboard options"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "dashboard-options"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`adminPath`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "adminpath"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The path the dashboard is served on, defaults to `/admin`. During development `withAlinea` forwards it to the local dashboard of `alinea dev`; `alinea build` writes the dashboard to `public/admin.html` plus a `public/admin/` folder of assets (named after the path), and `withAlinea` serves it from there. Media URLs live below it as well: `/admin/file/...`. It can't be `/`. It replaces the deprecated `dashboardFile` option of 1.x."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`preview`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "preview"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Shows a preview next to the editor. `true` loads your site in an iframe and updates it while editors type, see "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Live previews",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JjypBvxQ7B90PqTq2hAlkJYWhH",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "2YlBsRF2vZwxcS27oOSJYmQM37q"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ". You can also pass a React component that receives `{entry}` and renders the preview itself. Workspaces, roots and types accept the same `preview` option, the most specific one wins: `preview: false` on a type hides the preview for entries without a page, such as site settings."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`enableDrafts`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "enabledrafts"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Off by default: every save in the dashboard publishes right away. With `enableDrafts: true`:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Editors get a separate "
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Save draft",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": " action next to "
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Publish",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": ", and new entries start as drafts."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Published entries can be unpublished again."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "The published version stays live until the draft is published."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "The "
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "MCP server",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "link",
                      "_id": "3JkBBlK85abHv9fK3A6wmU1nggn",
                      "_link": "entry",
                      "_entry": "3JjyQUq7OEXLa3wIwCkEgiRasxN"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": " accepts `publish: false` to save drafts."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`roles`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "roles"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Custom roles with permission policies, see "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Roles and permissions",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JjypA5bA8uqLK8XSUyeAoFSIOr",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "3AhqfX37Pijf2zOEwYVVU4NmdHG"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ". An `admin` role is always added."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`maxUploadSize`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "maxuploadsize"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The maximum size of an uploaded file, in bytes, for example `20 * 1024 * 1024` for 20 MB. Larger uploads are refused with an error that names the limit. No limit by default."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Content delivery options"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "content-delivery-options"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`syncInterval`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "syncinterval"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "How your deployed site keeps its content fresh. The site checks the content revision of the repository and syncs right away when it changed; `syncInterval` is the fallback interval in seconds when that revision can't be determined. Defaults to `60`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "`0` syncs on every query."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "`Infinity` never syncs: the site only serves the content it was built with, and new content goes live with the next deploy."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "A single query can override it with `syncInterval`, or skip syncing with `disableSync: true`. See "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Instant publishing",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkBBlVr9jEUT5DOeAvaQzT4cFU",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "3JjNWhIOOARLjiO2HjeVoVyVN48"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`publicDir`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "publicdir"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The folder your site serves static files from, defaults to `public`. `alinea build` writes the dashboard into it, and media files stored inside it (the workspace `mediaDir`) are served from there."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`tracer`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "tracer"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "A function to instrument Alinea operations, for example with OpenTelemetry spans. It is called as `tracer(name, run)` and must return the result of `run()`. Errors thrown by the tracer itself are ignored, the operation still runs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "3JkCfgTracer000000000000001",
      "code": "import {trace} from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('alinea')\n\nexport const cms = createCMS({\n  // ...\n  tracer(name, run) {\n    return tracer.startActiveSpan(name, async span => {\n      try {\n        return await run()\n      } finally {\n        span.end()\n      }\n    })\n  }\n})",
      "fileName": "cms.ts",
      "language": "ts"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Good to know"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "good-to-know"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Environment variables"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "environment-variables"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`cms.ts` runs on the server and in the dashboard, which runs in the browser. In the dashboard only variables that start with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` or `PUBLIC_` are defined; other `process.env` values are `undefined` there and log a warning. Use a public variable for anything the config needs, such as the production URL, and keep secrets in the handler route instead."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The CLI reads `.env.local`, or `.env` when there is no `.env.local`, from the project folder or the nearest parent folder that has one. Variables already set in the environment win."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Splitting up the config"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "splitting-up-the-config"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Nothing requires one big file. Most projects keep each type in its own file and import them into `cms.ts`, for example `schema/Page.ts` or one folder per page type with its view component next to it, as the "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "tutorial",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkBBnleUlOEPaz6kBk2cEcDRci",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "3AONCC6cssRWNTfGBx86XSB2Exn"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " does. The config file itself only has to export `cms` as a named export, a default export is refused with `No export named cms found`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Dealing with errors"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "dealing-with-errors"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Your config file is compiled and executed by `alinea dev` and `alinea build`. An error thrown while loading it points to the compiled file:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2bRPtrWBR0pa60dm18O0y8DW2u8",
      "code": "Error: Fail\n    at file:///home/alineacms/alinea/node_modules/@alinea/generated/config.js?1706175675574:419:7\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:194:25)",
      "fileName": "",
      "language": "shellscript"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Alinea compiles your config with a source map. Enable Node's `--enable-source-maps` flag in your scripts to get positions in your own files:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2bRQUBTqZ510BRTvtbDs333cnoR",
      "code": "{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"NODE_OPTIONS=--enable-source-maps alinea dev -- next dev\",\n    \"build\": \"NODE_OPTIONS=--enable-source-maps alinea build -- next build\"\n  }\n}",
      "fileName": "",
      "language": "json"
    },
    {
      "_type": "NoticeBlock",
      "_id": "2bRQZBPfwzPF6lNUtjW0wVPFY06",
      "level": "info",
      "body": [
        {
          "_type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "text",
              "text": "If you're developing on Windows you can use "
            },
            {
              "_type": "text",
              "text": "cross-env",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "_type": "link",
                  "_id": "3JjypE032ZsmdNcMUIyalgHmMMT",
                  "_link": "url",
                  "href": "https://www.npmjs.com/package/cross-env"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_type": "text",
              "text": " to achieve the same."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The error now points to the right file:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2bRR5xvNhvfy0EaJAgL0owbuNYV",
      "code": "Error: Fail\n    at <anonymous> (/home/alinea/apps/dev/cms.ts:278:7)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:194:25)",
      "fileName": "",
      "language": "shellscript"
    }
  ],
